  "reading": "TWO different numbers. holdout_leak_fraction is ROW LEVEL: the share of held-out rows whose own latents come from a clip that is also in the fit. Those rows are near-duplicates of rows the refit saw, so a batch-row holdout score is part fit score; grouping by clip drives it to 0 and this probe asserts that. receptive_field_leak_fraction is the stronger question: the rows being split are mlp_in at this block, produced by DiT self-attention whose receptive field is the whole batch row, so a held-out row's activation is a function of EVERY clip in its batch row whatever clip it is filed under. Grouping by clip does not change that number at all -- only a clip-ALIGNED window does, one where each batch row is one whole clip. Read activation_independence: when it is false the clip-grouped holdout is a clean row-level split and still not an unseen-content error. Finally, two holdout SCORES from different groupings are not paired -- the splits hold out different rows, so the scores move for two reasons at once. Use holdout_decomposition.json, which scores ONE child on both splits.",
